# Local development/session artifacts - not part of the published tool
.claude/
.superpowers/
docs/superpowers/

# tests/ is intentionally excluded from the public GitHub repo (teammates
# don't need it to use the tool). It stays tracked here on `master` since
# it's already committed - this rule only matters when re-deriving a fresh
# `main` branch via `git checkout --orphan main && git add -A`, so that
# step doesn't accidentally re-include it.
tests/

# Bundled ffmpeg.exe/ffprobe.exe (~220MB each) so the tool works fully
# offline with zero setup. On this branch (`main`, what's published to
# GitHub) these are tracked via Git LFS instead of being ignored - see
# .gitattributes. GitHub rejects any single file over 100MB outright
# through a normal git push, hence LFS.
